stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> queued : POST /api/projects/{id}/scans (202 Accepted)

    queued --> crawling : Worker acquires ThreadPoolExecutor slot
    queued --> cancelled : User calls POST /api/scans/{id}/cancel before start
    queued --> failed : Pre-flight guardrail failure or unreachable target

    crawling --> scanning : Soft-404 calibrated & BFS endpoints persisted
    crawling --> cancelled : cancel_event.is_set() during crawl loop
    crawling --> failed : Fatal network loss or database write failure

    scanning --> completed : All selected checks finished & risk_score saved
    scanning --> cancelled : cancel_event.is_set() between checks or requests
    scanning --> failed : Unhandled orchestrator runtime error

    completed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]
    failed --> [*]

    note right of scanning
        Per-check exceptions are isolated inside
        try/except and emit check_warning events
        without transitioning the scan to failed.
    end note
